1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,940
Shall we go in? Let’s go! Welcome!

2
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:12,620
We are now entering the Sacred Heart Cultural Center of Montricoux.

3
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:19,020
As soon as you arrive, if you look up, you can see painted ceilings 

4
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:21,720
and a medallion directly above your head.

5
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:26,940
This place was originally a school of Christian art painting founded by Louis Cazottes.

6
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:31,100
When he was around thirty years old, he had a vision of the Sacred Heart and wondered what he should do

7
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:35,100
enter religious life or use his artistic knowledge differently.

8
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:39,160
He spoke about it with a priest, who told him that with such talent, 

9
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:40,660
he had something else to offer to the Catholic faith.

10
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:44,080
He had already started a small school in another village,

11
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:46,580
 but it was in Montricoux that he truly established this building.

12
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:50,080
Many well-known painters studied at the Sacred Heart school.

13
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:54,840
Among them were René Gaillard-Lala and Édouard Domergue-Lagarde,

14
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:58,000
who decorated many churches, especially around Toulouse.

15
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,860
If we look at the painted ceilings, we can see floral motifs.

16
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,640
While he was in Montricoux, he met an Italian painter.

17
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:09,080
There are many influences from Italian painters to whom he paid tribute.

18
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:13,260
You can see painters’ names and small medallions with their portraits in each corner.

19
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:16,420
And if you stand properly, with your back to the door, the view becomes beautiful.

20
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:19,980
I’m turning off the lights. If you come here, you should turn off the lights — that is when you see it best.

21
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:22,720
In the medallion on the left

22
00:01:22,830 --> 00:01:24,940
you can see the village of Montricoux represented there

23
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:26,860
and above, you can see angels

24
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:28,660
carrying the Sacred Heart

25
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:30,440
which gives the building its name, Sacred Heart

26
00:01:32,020 --> 00:01:32,900
as an offering.

27
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:34,920
Later, the building

28
00:01:34,950 --> 00:01:36,600
served many different purposes.

29
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:38,960
It housed unmarried mothers,

30
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:40,720
it became a cinema hall,

31
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:42,600
a theater rehearsal room,

32
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:43,500
even a gymnasium.

33
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,080
Then the media library opened in 2010.

34
00:01:47,439 --> 00:01:48,659
There we are, we can go inside.

35
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:59,620
To bring in light, something very common in Parisian studios,

36
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:00,500
there are very large windows.

37
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:02,960
Since this was a painting school, a great deal of light was necessary.

38
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:06,160
You can find the same thing upstairs, with identical windows.

39
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:09,160
And in what is now the corridor near the dance room,

40
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:13,420
there used to be large artists’ sinks for washing tools and paintbrushes.

41
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,720
The media library is on the ground floor,

42
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:21,940
upstairs, there are dance rooms, meeting rooms, art workshops, and the toy library office.

43
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:25,500
Around ten local associations regularly use the building.

44
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:29,000
There are dance classes, tai chi, yoga, and all sorts of activities.

45
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:31,000
There is also a transmission of popular culture here.

46
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:33,780
For example, on Fridays, knitters come here.

47
00:02:33,830 --> 00:02:37,420
It is not a club — they simply gather, knit, and share their knowledge.

48
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:44,420
We also welcome all the schoolchildren from the surrounding area — Montricoux, Vaïssac, Bruniquel — who come to the media library.

49
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:49,820
The goal is for them to make the library their own and feel it is a place where they belong and can return to.

50
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:52,660
Many of them later return with their parents just to spend time here.

51
00:02:53,070 --> 00:02:57,440
I love when a child opens the door and says, “Mom, come here, it’s this way!”

52
00:02:57,910 --> 00:02:59,920
And that truly makes me happy — mothers and fathers alike.
